{
 "version": 3,
 "set": "mobile",
 "scale_from_master": 0.25,
 "faces": "right",
 "referenceHeight": 98.2,
 "notes": [
  "All 19 animations show the bird at ONE size: the strips were normalised (normalise.py), so switching animations never changes its size. Never rescale one animation on its own.",
  "Frame n is at x = (n-1) * frameWidth. Every frame of a sheet is the same size.",
  "Standing sheets are pinned on the feet: anchor = where the toes meet the surface. Put it on the perch, 1 CSS px into it.",
  "Flying sheets are pinned on the eye: anchor = the eye. Move the eye along the flight path; rotate about it to bank.",
  "Mirror (scaleX -1 about the anchor) to face left, but never a standing bird from one frame to the next: use `turn`. In the air, mirror only while banked edge-on (glide 4).",
  "Size: drawScale = targetHeightCss / referenceHeight, where referenceHeight is the standing look-around bird in sheet px. Headline: target = 1.0 x the headline font size. Island: target = 200 art px x stage.project(...).scale.",
  "eye[] gives the eye per frame (sheet px) where it is visible, for hand-overs and for keeping cross-fades aligned.",
  "eye[] corrected by hand after the first measure caught dark feathers: closed eyes are null, flap 1 and hover 6 are the pinned eye."
 ],
 "perchRule": "Only perch where both feet land: a flat top at least 14 CSS px wide with no taller ink within 22 CSS px either side. Never on a pointed or V-shaped top (M, A, W, V, N), a thin stem (I, L), an H crossbar, the tent finial, a pawn, the lantern. See perches.js and island_perches.json.",
 "crossfade": {
  "betweenAnimationsMs": 125,
  "withinStandingStripMs": 42,
  "onlyIfSilhouetteOverlap": 0.7,
  "how": "draw the new frame at full opacity, then the previous frame on top at 0.6 -> 0.35 -> 0.15 (24 fps ticks); shift the old frame by how far the eye moved. Skip it when the two poses overlap less than 70 % (a clean cut reads better than a double image)."
 },
